            <div xml:id="d834">

                <pb facs="1052" n="938" xml:id="pg938"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">325.1121 Bethune, Larry K./46</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-21">April 21, 1931</date>.<lb/>[Received May
                        2.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 845</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to this Embassy’s
                    despatch No. 819 of March 27, 1931,<anchor n="25" xml:id="d834-f1"/> with
                    special reference to enclosure No. 6, and to report that the Chilean Supreme
                    Court, on April 21st, and by a vote of four to one, denied the appeal of
                    Brusadelli y Manni from the decision of the Court of Appeals. By the latter
                    decision, made on March 21, 1931, the Court of Appeals acted favorably on the
                    appeal (similar to habeas corpus) presented by the attorneys for General Motors
                    on behalf of Mr. Bethune, who was released and whose bond was cancelled.</p>
                <p>This decision of the Supreme Court confirms the justice of the Embassy’s protest
                    against the illegality of the arrest of Mr. Bethune and of his being held <hi
                        rendition="#italic">incomunicado.</hi></p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. Henry Norweb</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
